  <h1>About this project</h1>
  <p class="lede"><i>{{ site.title }}</i> was created by {{ site.creator }}.</p>
  <p>[Describe the project, who runs it, and how lists are chosen and transcribed.]</p>

  <h2>Subscriber lists</h2>
  <p>Many books were financed in advance by readers who pledged to buy a copy. Their names — often grouped by town, sometimes with the number of copies — were printed in the book itself.</p>

  <h2>Donation lists</h2>
  <p>Printed or manuscript records of gifts to a cause — a congregation, a charity, a relief fund — usually giving the donor, sometimes their town, and the amount. Gifts were often paid through an agent: a bank, a bookseller or a local collector, printed as “per Messrs. …”.</p>

  <h2>How entries are recorded</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><b>Name as printed</b> is kept exactly as it appears, including titles and spellings.</li>
    <li><b>Identified as</b> links the entry to a person or organization record once an editor is confident. Different printed forms of the same name are grouped on that record.</li>
    <li><b>Amounts</b> are kept in the original currency and units (for example £ s. d.). They are not converted between currencies.</li>
    <li>Readings marked <span class="cert cert-prob">~</span> are probable and <span class="cert">?</span> uncertain.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Using and citing the data</h2>
  <p>All data can be <a href="/data/">downloaded as CSV</a>. Each list, person, organization and place has a stable address you can cite. {{ site.license }}.</p>

